# --- Enum rows that are live data, not dead names ---------------------------
#   ModeQuality / ModeLowBitrate / ModeAggressive (subsync/vad) — NOT zero-value
#     sentinels. Each names a live row of the production vadModes table
#     (vad.go:94-99), selected by newVADInst's `vadModes[int(mode)]` and
#     reachable through the exported FramesBinaryThresholdTuned, which
#     audio_sync.go:267 calls with a caller-chosen Mode. vad_bench_test.go:9
#     benchmarks all four. Production presets pick ModeVeryAggressive today;
#     the other rows stay callable, and deleting the constants would leave the
#     table rows unnameable.
#   TransformNone (subsync) — the documented zero value of TransformKind, and
#     the iota anchor. Every Transform{} that carries no descriptor has
#     Kind == TransformNone, which Transform.Digest renders through its default
#     branch as "none" — a value the golden corpus artifacts admit. Deleting it
#     would renumber TransformShift to 0 and make the zero transform digest as
#     "shift(0ms)", silently changing the corpus and the voting log.
constant ModeQuality
constant ModeLowBitrate
constant ModeAggressive
constant TransformNone
